  "task": {
    "objective": "Maintain and trade between four settlements while choosing resource investments, levee/culvert routing, raised roads and shared flood responses during a persistent 20x20 interaction window.",
    "natural_termination": "No single settlement quest ends this persistent strategy world. terminated remains false and tick 384 truncates; harvest, trade, construction and flood losses never reset the state.",
    "interaction": "Levees and closed culverts divert physical packets toward neighboring fields. Roads allow deep-water crossings and faster hauling but degrade in severe water. Grain trade and material gifts change other settlements' future construction/food options; dated reports require physical inspection or adjacent transfer.",
    "observation_access": "Public information consists of clock/terminal causes, rain, aggregate flood-alert count, settlement coordinates and fixed food valuations. Each worker sees map cells, peers and water packets within Manhattan radius four; hidden map/entity records are -1 with a visibility bit. Own settlement stores/field water are continuously available as its explicit home telemetry; other settlement contents require local visibility. Each actor additionally sees its own dated report memory and six reward components. Public safety rewards and the alerts counter reveal only the aggregate exposed-settlement count, not remote identities or crop/store values. The scene map uses the actual map_visible mask."
